## Rocci OKF CLI

### Validate knowledge bundle

```sh
cargo run -p rocci-okf -- check [ROOT] [--profile base|rocci] [--format terminal|json]
```

Base mode checks OKF v0.2. Rocci mode additionally validates approved types,
tags, lifecycle, provenance, authority, and owner fields.

### Inspect knowledge catalog, concept, and graph

```sh
cargo run -p rocci-okf -- inspect concept ID [ROOT] [--profile base|rocci]
cargo run -p rocci-okf -- inspect catalog [ROOT] [--profile base|rocci]
cargo run -p rocci-okf -- inspect graph [ROOT] [--profile base|rocci]
```

### Search knowledge records

```sh
cargo run -p rocci-okf -- search QUERY [ROOT] [--profile base|rocci]
```

### Retrieval benchmarks

```sh
cargo run -p rocci-okf -- benchmark BENCHMARK_FILE [ROOT] [--profile base|rocci]
```

Measures top-5 hit rate and mean reciprocal rank against versioned questions and
enforces passing thresholds.

### Live review preview server

```sh
cargo run -p rocci-okf -- run [PATH] [--profile base|rocci] [--port PORT] [--no-window]
```

`PATH` may be a bundle directory, a concept Markdown file inside a bundle, or
the bundle-root `index.md`. A concept file opens the review site on that
record. The preview window supports current-document find and `Cmd/Ctrl-K`
jump-to-record using `/catalog.json`. The Dev control opens a panel at
`/__rocci/dev` with Performance, Source, and Console tabs for the current
route. Collection indexes and `/review/` have inspect snapshots. Original
Markdown and built HTML highlight with `tok-*` classes. Unavailable OKF AST
and Roc views show a reason on the Source tab.

### Build static review artifacts

```sh
cargo run -p rocci-okf -- build [ROOT] [--output DIRECTORY] [--profile base|rocci]
```

---

## Project browser

`rocci-browser` is a fourth binary, not a `rocci` subcommand. See
[Project browser](/docs/guides/rocci-browser/) for Cmd-P versus Cmd-K, the
registry file, and that `rocci browse` is the component gallery.

This repo's `.rocci/browser.toml` execs `target/debug` product CLIs with
`browser-adapter`. Build those binaries before the host:

```sh
cargo build -p rocci-browser -p rocci-cli -p rocci-rocdown-cli -p rocci-okf
cargo run -q -p rocci-browser
cargo run -q -p rocci-browser -- add ./my-project
cargo run -q -p rocci-browser -- open TARGET [--document ID] [--no-window] [--json]
```

`--no-window --json` prints `{ "url", "title" }` for agents and for machines
without a display. There is no `tui` command.

On macOS, `./scripts/bundle-browser-macos.sh` (or `rocci-browser package`)
assembles an ad-hoc **Rocci Browser.app**. That wrapper is not `rocci bundle`.
Production signing is planned.

